    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for spotting this. The docstring is wrong.<br>\nThe idea is that if the category <code>C</code> had a terminal object <code>T</code>, the <code>Y i</code> could be interpreted as family of objects over <code>T</code>, they would generate a sieve of <code>T</code>, and then for any <code>X : C</code>, we could consider the pullback of this sieve by the unique map from <code>X</code> to <code>T</code>: the resulting sieve should coincide with <code>ofObjects X Y</code> (this is not explicitly stated, but <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Sieve.pullback_ofObjects#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Sieve.pullback_ofObjects</a> is enough to convince me that this is true).<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41819\">#41819</a></p>",
        "id": 611077003,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1784210002
